## Official coursework summary (Web Application Development 2, 2025/26)

**Weighting:** Written report **30%** · Practical **70%** · Submission **12:00 noon 8 April** (per specification).

**Module learning outcomes (relevant):** design/develop/test/deploy a data-driven web app; authentication; security awareness; architectures/frameworks; critical evaluation of MVC.

### Practical (70%) — Yoga & Mindfulness Studio booking site

**Stack (baseline):** Node.js, Express, NeDB-promises, Mustache (from supplied prototype: `https://github.com/FionaMacRaeFairlie/WAD2_posscw_2526---Start.git`).

**Required behaviour**

- **Not logged in:** information/overview page (organisation, classes, location); view **current and upcoming** courses with per-class: **name**, **duration**, **date/time**, **description**, **location**, **price**.
- **Registered users:** **enrol** in a course or **book** a class.
- **Organisers (logged in):** add courses/classes; **delete** courses/classes; **update** class details; **generate class list** with participant names; **add/delete organisers**; **remove users**.

**Submissions (practical)**

- Code; **README** (how to run; **list of implemented features**).
- **CodeGrade** on GCULearn: `.zip` or GitHub link.
- **~15 min video** (Planet eStream): demo, design/development approach, **decision-making with an AI assistant**, features, **security** and how addressed; **do not use AI to generate the video**.
- **Link to deployed** site.

**AI use (Level 3 collaboration on Perkins et al. scale):** may assist with **code** but student must **evaluate, modify**, and **explain** generated code. **Not** acceptable: AI-generated **report** or **video**; **spelling/grammar check** for the report is allowed.

**Markers’ summary:** full functionality (listings, details, enrolment, organiser CRUD, role-based access); **clean, accessible, responsive** UI; **reliable auth** and secure handling; show **understanding** and **refinement** of AI-assisted code; **deployment** or clear install docs.

### Written report (30%) — ~**2000 words**

Critically evaluate the **supplied** prototype (not only your changes):

- **System design:** compare to **classic MVC**; argue whether approach is **optimal** for this app type.
- **Completeness:** what the spec requires vs what the supplied code **covers** vs **missing**.
- **Code quality:** **JavaScript** and **Mustache** templates.
- **Test coverage** of supplied tests (quantify where possible; gaps and improvements).

